%T A395083 205578547591329,74675907271804450,37774102272743767799
%N A395083 Number of relations R on an n-element set such that the transitive closure of R has exactly one element more than R.
%C A395083 The terms were computed by decomposing transitive relations into labeled posets with blocks corresponding to their equivalence classes, and using the numbers of comparable and cover pairs in these posets. Unlabeled posets and their automorphism groups were used to obtain the required labeled counts. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 28 2026
%H A395083 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transitive_closure">Transitive closure</a>
%e A395083 For n=0,1 the only relation is transitive (or has no missing pair to add), so a(0) = a(1) = 0.
%Y A395083 Cf. A006905.
